      "sourceErrata": [
        "7A 11(b): the final rationalisation multiplies numerator and denominator by cos x.",
        "7A 12: SolutionBank gives the positive cosh branch. The nonnegative inverse-cosh argument, negative branch and constant solutions are made explicit.",
        "7A 13(a): the printed working only parameterises positive solutions. C exp(sinh x) also includes the negative and zero solutions.",
        "7A 15(a): multiplying by sec x must give y sec x tan x, preserving the sec x factor missing from a SolutionBank line.",
        "7A 16: SolutionBank assumes a ≠ 0. The two degenerate a = 0 cases follow the displayed textbook equation.",
        "7C 2(b) and 6(a): use homogeneous equations with the coefficients in the textbook. SolutionBank opening lines contain stale coefficients.",
        "7C 3(b): 2μ − 6λ = 1 with μ = 1/36 gives λ = −17/108. The bank drops this minus sign going from its own intermediate line to its solution.",
        "7D 1(b): keep A on exp(−2x) and B on exp(−3x) throughout rather than silently exchanging the constants as in the bank. Final result agrees.",
        "7D 8(a)(i): textbook prints the trial as y = λt³exp(2t) for an equation in x; preserve y in the question then use x in the working.",
        "7D 12: differentiating μx sin 3x twice contributes +6μ cos 3x, so μ is fixed at zero. The derivative of −x cos(3x)/6 contains +x sin(3x)/2. Final particular solution agrees with SolutionBank.",
        "7D 13(b): use derivative sign on both sides of the unique stationary time to establish a global maximum."
      ],
